			"notes": "# AE2 Objects 0.2.1\n\nChanges since `0.2.0`.\n\n## Added\n\n- Minecraft `26.2` and `26.3` builds, alongside the existing `26.1.2` build.\n- Separate release jars for each supported Minecraft version, so players only install the jar that matches their game.\n\n## Changed\n\n- Item and fluid housings now use distinct recipes:\n  - Item recipes use an amethyst block.\n  - Fluid recipes use a copper block.\n  - The housing centre remains empty for the storage component.\n- All quartz glass in the direct-cell and housing recipes is now Vibrant Quartz Glass.\n- NeoForge and Applied Energistics 2 versions are pinned per Minecraft version through the version catalog.\n\n## Fixed\n\n- Added the 26.3 inventory/drop prediction API compatibility layer.\n- Split the creative-menu clone hook between `AbstractContainerMenu` on 26.1.2 and `Slot.safeClone` on 26.2+.\n- Added 26.3 data-generation event support and advancement format conversion.\n- Isolated 26.3 datagen output so it cannot overwrite the canonical 26.1 recipe data.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The `26.2` and `26.3` builds currently require Applied Energistics 2 alpha releases.\n- MEGA Cells `1m`–`256m` support remains disabled until a MEGA Cells 26.x build exists.\n- Applied Mekanistics chemical support remains inactive until an appmek 26.x build exists.\n- Install only the jar matching your Minecraft version.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/Likos-Lupus/AE2Objects/compare/0.2.0...0.2.1"
		},
