			"notes": "# AE2Objects 0.2.0\n\nChanges since `0.1.0+26.1.2`.\n\n## Added\n\n- Deep fluid storage cells for ME drives and chests, covering 1k through 256k tiers.\n- Portable deep storage cells for items and fluids, covering 1k through 256k tiers.\n- Portable-cell battery/menu integration, FE energy capability, charged creative variants, and Void upgrade support.\n- Catalog-driven deep-cell registration with item and fluid channel bindings.\n\n## Changed\n\n- Deep-cell storage was reorganized into domain, channel, persistence, inventory, and client-snapshot layers.\n- Existing 1k–256k item cells keep their registry IDs, data components, and saved-data format.\n- Deep-cell tooltips now use NeoForge's `RegisterTooltipAppendersEvent`; family, UUID, capacity, partition, and portable energy lines are preserved.\n- Storage hot paths now cache total amounts, use bounded top-ten previews, encode and preview in one pass, defer filter/context creation, and fast-path nested-cell checks.\n- Fluid cell colors were adjusted for the fluid series.\n- Development artifacts include the commit hash; release artifacts use `ae2objects-0.2.0+26.1.2.jar`.\n\n## Fixed\n\n- Server cell context is resolved per thread; client and pre-server code no longer touches the server repository.\n- Recovered cells are dropped when the player's inventory is full instead of being lost.\n- Clone operations without a server context create an independent client-side identity without repository access.\n- Saved-data snapshots are exposed read-only.\n\n## Internal\n\n- Added Stonecutter-based builds, release packaging, CI build workflow, Dependabot configuration, and expanded documentation.\n\n## Notes\n\n- MEGA Cells 1m–256m support is disabled in 0.2.0: no items are registered and no recipes are generated. It will be re-enabled once a MEGA Cells 26.1 build is available.\n- Applied Mekanistics chemical support remains inactive until an appmek 26.1 build exists.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/Likos-Lupus/AE2Objects/compare/0.1.0%2B26.1.2...0.2.0"
		},
